      "source": [
        "### Distinct-n (diversidad léxica)\n",
        "\n",
        "Se tokeniza cada reseña y se calculan n-gramas. Distinct-n se define como:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `Distinct-n = (# n-gramas únicos) / (# n-gramas totales)`\n",
        "\n",
        "En este notebook se reportan Distinct-1 y Distinct-2 por modelo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DDyIOPz1xNsb"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import nltk\n",
        "nltk.download(\"punkt\")\n",
        "nltk.download(\"punkt_tab\")\n",
        "from nltk.tokenize import word_tokenize\n",
        "from nltk import ngrams\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from tqdm import tqdm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4NmhA05hzW-u"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "def distinct_n(texts, n):\n",
        "    # Agrega todos los n-gramas (n=1,2,...) de todas las reseñas y calcula la proporción de únicos.\n",
        "    all_ngrams = []\n",
        "    for text in texts:\n",
        "        tokens = word_tokenize(text.lower())\n",
        "        all_ngrams.extend(list(ngrams(tokens, n)))\n",
        "    return len(set(all_ngrams)) / len(all_ngrams) if all_ngrams else 0.0\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mzYB1d_XzXkN"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Calcular Distinct-n por modelo\n",
        "results = []\n",
        "for model_name, group in df.groupby(\"model\"):\n",
        "    texts = group[\"text\"].dropna().tolist()\n",
        "    results.append({\n",
        "        \"model\": model_name,\n",
        "        \"distinct_1\": distinct_n(texts, 1),\n",
        "        \"distinct_2\": distinct_n(texts, 2),\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "distinct_df = pd.DataFrame(results).sort_values(\"model\").reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "distinct_df[[\"distinct_1\", \"distinct_2\"]] = distinct_df[[\"distinct_1\", \"distinct_2\"]].round(4)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Fd58KWsNzZck"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Mostrar resultados agregados\n",
        "display(distinct_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Guardar archivos (dataset generado y resultados de Distinct-n)\n",
        "df.to_csv(\"generated_reviews.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "distinct_df.to_csv(\"distinct_results.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Archivos guardados: generated_reviews.csv, distinct_results.csv\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6J6hsz9IYPdb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### TF-IDF + similitud coseno (diversidad de contenido)\n",
        "\n",
        "Este bloque mide similitud entre reseñas usando:\n",
        "- Representación TF-IDF sobre n-gramas (1,2)\n",
        "- Similitud coseno entre todas las parejas\n",
        "\n",
        "Se calculan dos métricas por modelo:\n",
        "- `avg_max_similarity`: para cada reseña, se busca su reseña más similar (excluyéndose a sí misma) y se promedia.\n",
        "- `near_duplicate_rate`: proporción de reseñas cuyo mejor match supera un umbral (por defecto 0.90)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "V3pU-RYMbrlz"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n",
        "\n",
        "# Lectura del dataset generado.\n",
        "# Nota: aquí se usa una ruta de ejemplo /content/sample_data/... (típica de Colab).\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(\"/content/sample_data/generated_reviews.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def near_duplicate_metrics(texts, threshold=0.90):\n",
        "    # Calcula similitudes y detecta reseñas muy parecidas (near-duplicates) según un umbral.\n",
        "    texts = [str(t) for t in texts]\n",
        "    if len(texts) < 2:\n",
        "        return np.nan, np.nan\n",
        "\n",
        "    # TF-IDF sobre uni+bi-gramas para capturar palabras y pequeñas frases\n",
        "    vec = TfidfVectorizer(ngram_range=(1, 2), min_df=1)\n",
        "    X = vec.fit_transform(texts)\n",
        "\n",
        "    sim = cosine_similarity(X)\n",
        "    np.fill_diagonal(sim, -1)  # ignorar similitud consigo mismo\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Para cada reseña: similitud máxima con otra reseña\n",
        "    max_sim = sim.max(axis=1)\n",
        "    avg_max_sim = float(np.mean(max_sim))\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Porcentaje de reseñas cuyo mejor match supera el umbral (near-duplicates)\n",
        "    near_dup_rate = float(np.mean(max_sim >= threshold))\n",
        "\n",
        "    return avg_max_sim, near_dup_rate\n",
        "\n",
        "rows = []\n",
        "for model, g in df.groupby(\"model\"):\n",
        "    per_prompt = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Se calcula por escenario (product/persona/rating) para no mezclar contextos distintos.\n",
        "    for _, gg in g.groupby([\"product\", \"persona\", \"rating\"]):\n",
        "        per_prompt.append(near_duplicate_metrics(gg[\"text\"].tolist(), threshold=0.90))\n",
        "\n",
        "    rows.append({\n",
        "        \"model\": model,\n",
        "        \"avg_max_similarity\": np.mean([x[0] for x in per_prompt]),\n",
        "        \"near_duplicate_rate\": np.mean([x[1] for x in per_prompt]),\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "neardup_df = pd.DataFrame(rows).sort_values(\"model\").reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "display(neardup_df)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
